  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Grate carrot.\n• Trim and cut green beans into thirds.\n• Cut firm tofu (see ingredients) into 1cm pieces."
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a large saucepan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat.\n• Cook green beans, tossing regularly, until tender, 4-5 minutes.\n• Transfer to a bowl and set aside."
    },
    {
      "text": "• Return saucepan to high heat with a drizzle of olive oil. Cook carrot and tofu, stirring, until tender, 2-3 minutes.\n• Reduce heat to medium, then add Bengal curry paste (see ingredients)and Mumbai spice blend, and cook until fragrant, 1-2 minutes.\n• Stir in basmati rice, the water and vegetable stock powder, bring to boil.\n• Cover and reduce heat to medium-low. Cook for 12 minutes, then remove pan from heat.\n• Keep covered until rice is tender and the water is absorbed, 15 minutes. TIP: The rice will finish cooking in its own steam, so don't peek!"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Once rice has finished cooking, stir through green beans and baby spinach leaves, until wilted and combined. Season to taste.\n• Divide Indian tofu and veggie biryani between bowls. Top with tamarind chutney and Greek-style yogurt.\n• Sprinkle over flaked almonds to serve. Enjoy!"
    }
  ]
